# Light and dark reports: CSI ? 996 n asks, CSI ? 2031 h asks to be told of changes.
# Contour's "Color palette update notifications" is the specification; the host's scheme is a step.

test a program asking for the color scheme is told dark
spec contour color-palette-update-notifications: CSI ? 996 n is answered CSI ? 997 ; 1 n for dark
size 10 4
color-scheme dark
feed \e[?996n
reply \e[?997;1n

test a program asking for the color scheme is told light
spec contour color-palette-update-notifications: CSI ? 997 ; 2 n is light mode
size 10 4
color-scheme light
feed \e[?996n
reply \e[?997;2n

test a terminal that was not told its scheme does not answer
convention a program has to cope with terminals that stay silent; guessing would be a lie
size 10 4
feed \e[?996n\e[5n
reply \e[0n

test a change is reported to a program that asked to hear of changes
spec contour color-palette-update-notifications: with mode 2031 set the terminal sends the report when the scheme changes
size 10 4
color-scheme dark
feed \e[?2031h
reply none
color-scheme light
reply \e[?997;2n
color-scheme dark
reply \e[?997;1n

test a change nobody asked to hear of is not reported, and telling the same scheme again is no change
spec contour color-palette-update-notifications: the DSR is sent when the mode is set and the scheme changed
size 10 4
color-scheme dark
color-scheme light
reply none
feed \e[?2031h
color-scheme light
reply none
feed \e[?2031l
color-scheme dark
reply none

test mode 2031 is a mode a program can ask about
spec xterm ctlseqs DECRQM: CSI ? Ps $ p is answered CSI ? Ps ; Pm $ y
size 10 4
feed \e[?2031$p\e[?2031h\e[?2031$p
reply \e[?2031;2$y\e[?2031;1$y
